---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const description =
  'How GamersXpress stories are reported: official announcements and reputable sources, claims checked against cited sources, rumors labeled.';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Policy | GamersXpress"
  description={description}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'GamersXpress', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Editorial Policy', path: '/editorial-policy' },
  ]}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">Editorial policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      GamersXpress stories are based on official announcements and reputable
      sources, and every claim is checked against the sources cited in the
      article.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">Sources</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      We start from primary sources where possible: company and studio
      announcements, official blogs, press releases, and documentation. When
      other outlets are part of the story, they are treated as sources too and
      linked like any other.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">Checking claims</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      Before an article is published, its claims are checked against the
      sources cited in it. A claim that cannot be supported by a source does
      not appear as fact.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">Rumors</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      Unconfirmed information is labeled as a rumor or left out entirely. We
      never state a rumor as fact, and only confirmed pricing and availability
      appear as fact.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">Sources in every article</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      Every article ends with a Sources section linking the material it was
      built from, so you can check anything yourself.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">Corrections</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      When we fix an error, the article shows an Updated date. See
      <a
        href="/corrections"
        class="text-sky-600 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-sky-500 dark:text-sky-400 dark:hover:text-sky-300"
        >corrections</a
      >
      for how to report one. Articles also follow our
      <a
        href="/ai-disclosure"
        class="text-sky-600 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-sky-500 dark:text-sky-400 dark:hover:text-sky-300"
        >AI disclosure</a
      >.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
